+# Sparse terminal discovery version 1
+
+2026-10-21. The user authorized an isolated combined implementation and a fresh
+M1 exploratory run if mechanism checks pass. This supersedes the earlier
+design-only stopping point for this branch; it changes no existing study.
+
+The retained core supplies formal request/confirmation, generic Boolean scripts,
+typed terminal measurement, legal primitive bindings and ordinary residual credit.
+The fresh organism has five control vertices, zero reader definitions and zero
+scoring conditions, with one shared zero bias. It does not call the selective
+initializer or create its 42+38 equality banks.
+
+Version 1 deliberately uses the existing finite equality-reader family: a reader
+chooses a typed coordinate/value test; one-to-three readers form AND, OR or
+exactly-one scripts. These are generic supplied operators. Discovery selects
+coordinate/value regions and useful compositions, not a new operator vocabulary
+or continuous prototype-learning law. There is no supplied state/action partition
+or feature-name interpretation. A richer reader family remains a separate test.
+
+## Birth and prospective admission
+
+At the first real selected action the organism samples at most 16 trial masks.
+Only their selected-binding measurements are obtained through formal terminals.
+Half the proposal opportunities may extend an existing live or immature mask
+with another sampled coordinate; the rest sample fresh masks. No marginal
+maturity requirement blocks jointly useful trials. Trials persist at most 256
+actual observations; all definitions and evidence survive as history after exit.
+
+The first 32 actual observations fit a residual offset on active occurrences.
+That offset then freezes. Later receipts compare the actual saved prediction
+against that prediction plus the frozen offset when the candidate is active.
+The first prospective score needs 32 later observations and at least four active
+occurrences in each window. Mean squared-error reduction minus 0.0001 per reader
+is nomination evidence, not causal policy value. Negative useful offsets qualify.
+
+Every 32 observations, at most one zero-weight contribution is admitted. With
+probability .25 the choice can be exploratory among supported proposals,
+including not-yet-completely-reviewed ones; a fully reviewed nonpositive score
+vetoes this route. Otherwise the best positive prospective score is selected.
+No fitted offset is installed as an action weight. Subsequent actual behavior
+must learn the new coefficient through ordinary residual credit.
+
+## Credit and retirement
+
+Only bias and the actual selected active scoring conditions receive
+alpha*(reward-saved_prediction)/(1+active_conditions), with alpha=.3. Probes
+never enter this denominator or receive real action credit. Exploration=.25 is
+unchanged. Bias fast/slow transfer preserves its effective sum and is not called
+retention protection.
+
+Live terms accumulate pre-update leave-one-out prediction gains on selected
+receipts. At age 256, a complete 128-receipt window with at least four active
+receipts and mean gain below minus the resource charge may retire one term per
+boundary. Other removal evidence resets after a scoring-structure change.
+This is an observational predictive-removal hypothesis, not guaranteed safe
+retention. Coefficient magnitude alone is not a removal rule.
+
+Readers used by any live or trial script remain instantiated. Boundary rebuilds
+reclaim only orphan physical probe/readers, preserving surviving weights and
+retired hypothesis history. Limits are 96 live scoring conditions, 16 trials and
+8192 physical nodes. A genuine budget/semantic failure aborts rather than quietly
+falling back to another chooser.
+
+## Scope of the first M1 run
+
+The initial chess pilot uses the unchanged declared 16-coordinate geometric
+feature space and only actual selected-move outcomes. This isolates dynamic
+reader/composition discovery; it does not claim a raw-board learned sensor basis.
+All learning stays plastic. One prospectively pinned fresh seed and fixed budget
+make an exploratory run, not a reliability, superiority or autonomous general
+script-induction result. Failed learning is preserved without parameter tuning.
+
+Mated positions have no legal move and do not fit this action interface. Mate-in-0
+recognition is recorded as a separate future observation/goal-detection task,
+with completed-state outcomes and nonmated controls. An independently learned
+recognizer could later make fallible predictions on imagined feature frames.
+It must not query hypothetical environment checkmate labels or turn imagined
+outcomes into real reinforcement. This packet does not implement that interface.
+
+The M1 pilot already records each actual after-position and its real outcome.
+Those observed successful and unsuccessful after-positions could later ground
+an M0 recognition task without asking for hypothetical labels. Positive mated
+examples alone would permit an always-confirming detector, so nonmated and
+stalemate controls matter. Minimizing a recognizer is a subsequent compression
+question; this first run does not teach it a supplied checkmate predicate.
