+# Sparse discovery: one exploratory native M1 pilot
+
+The runner `tools/sparse_discovery_m1_pilot.py` exercises the opt-in discovery
+organism. It does not change the production initializer, credit law or M2.
+
+The scientific identity is seed `202610210901`, 3,072 actual one-move training
+attempts: 2,048 acquisition actions and 1,024 continuation actions. An independent
+schedule RNG samples the known 1,512-position M1 population uniformly. Preparation
+exports only FEN strings from the two existing regression-receipt files; their
+saved actions and rewards never enter the organism.
+
+The actor begins with five generic physical interface/controller vertices,
+one zero-weight bias, no readers and no scoring conditions. The declared
+16-coordinate geometric schema remains a substantial supplied embodiment prior.
+New sparse proposals use only the declared coordinate types/domains and their
+own later selected-action observations.
+
+## What an admission means
+
+Admission means a proposal becomes a zero-weight scoring contributor. Ordinary
+subsequent selected-action residual credit determines its actual influence.
+It does not mean causal usefulness, mature competence or successful behavior.
+
+Admission reasons are reported separately as `exploratory` and
+`prospective_prediction`. With the defaults, exploratory admission can occur
+at the first 32-observation boundary after sufficient discovery activation,
+before any prospective validation observations. The report separately counts
+admissions before a complete prospective review. Do not call every admission
+"relevance confirmed". A positive reviewed prediction gain is also predictive
+evidence, not a causal intervention or demonstrated behavioral improvement.
+
+## Evidence and verification scope
+
+The producer saves complete action/outcome, credit, lifecycle and inventory
+records; native checkpoints at actions 0/512/1024/1536/2048/2560/3072; and greedy
+full-population censuses at 0/1536/2048/3072 using disposable actor copies.
+
+A fresh process reconstructs every training choice, selected outcome and
+development event. Separate scalar arithmetic checks the prediction and every
+active/inactive credit recipient before consolidation/development. Checkpoint
+comparison covers the **declared behavioral/development snapshot**, not every
+physical or historical field. Complete pickled checkpoints remain saved and
+hash-bound; cold continuations compare actual subsequent behavior and the same
+declared snapshot. Transient graph request states/activations and omitted
+historical fields are not independently compared. This limitation must remain
+explicit in the final report.
+
+One actor and four sampled censuses cannot establish continuous retention,
+seed reliability, unseen-position generalization or the advantage of the
+relevance selector over matched random development.
+
+## Operational boundary
+
+The default complete ceiling is four hours, including a real second native
+replay and sealing. Production receives at most half of the substantive clock;
+five minutes remain reserved for sealing. Both phases have sampled 2 GiB RSS
+guards and suspension-inclusive wall deadlines. These are enforced limits,
+not a guarantee that every possible grown trajectory completes. Short-worker
+RSS samples are sampled observations, not exact high-water memory measurements.
+
+The output directory and scientific identity claim are exclusive. Failure
+preserves the partial evidence; changing output paths does not free the seed
+for another scientific attempt. A harmless child first qualifies actual RSS
+sampling. Sandbox permission for `/bin/ps` is therefore needed before science.
+The runner owns and cleans its child process groups and optional idle-sleep
+assertion. Source pins cover actual imported repository/chess modules and the
+interpreter binary; unrelated historical trees are not traversed.
+
+## Engineering evidence
+
+`runner-engineering-001` produced 32 engineering actions but failed replay on a
+tuple/list JSON comparison defect. The original source bytes were reconstructed
+by reverting that single comparison and matched exactly to the original source
+SHA256, then saved append-only under its `historical-source/` directory. Original
+records, failures and original checksum inventory were not edited.
+
+`runner-engineering-002` independently verified the same 32-event engineering
+stream, three checkpoints, two cold continuations and two eight-position censuses.
+Its original runner bytes were also preserved before these reporting-only
+clarifications. Neither engineering attempt consumes the scientific identity or
+establishes M1 learning benefit. Focused tests cover credit corruption, checkpoint
+hash corruption, source changes, input isolation, JSON representation and
+deadline/memory cleanup; unit guard tests inject RSS samples, while engineering
+execution obtains actual owned-child samples.
