+# First sparse discovery native M1 pilot
+
+Prospective protocol, 2026-10-21. The user's latest request authorizes this
+isolated implementation and an M1 training run if mechanical checks pass. It
+supersedes the previous investigation handoff's design-only stopping point.
+No existing learner defaults, M1/M2 studies or historical evidence are changed.
+
+## Question and interpretation
+
+Can one fresh native organism, starting without instantiated input readers or
+scoring conditions, acquire useful M1 behavior while dynamically proposing,
+reviewing, admitting and retaining its own sparse reader/composition population?
+
+This is one exploratory trajectory. It is not a paired superiority study,
+population-reliability result, full sensor-family discovery or an adoption gate.
+The old M1 milestone remains the supplied-vocabulary behavioral reference.
+
+The fresh graph has five generic control nodes, one shared zero bias, zero
+conditions/readers and no pretrained prefix. The unchanged 16-coordinate
+geometric feature space is explicitly supplied embodiment. Finite equality
+readers and AND/OR/exactly-one scripts are generic supplied grammar. Neither
+relevant coordinates nor a mating formula is supplied. All new parameters and
+decisions obey SPARSE_DISCOVERY_DESIGN.md; ordinary alpha=.3, epsilon=.25 and
+selected-action residual credit remain fixed.
+
+## Prelaunch mechanism evidence
+
+The independent design review found no launch-blocking information leak or
+credit defect. Focused checks cover the fresh population, native terminal and
+action authority, unchanged active/inactive recipients, strict prospective
+windows, negative offsets, young joint trials, dependencies/history, retirement,
+checkpoint continuation and guard failure modes.
+
+Two small native runner attempts used a distinct engineering seed. Attempt001
+preserves a tuple/list serialization-comparison defect; attempt002 reconstructed
+32 actions, three checkpoints, two cold continuations and two eight-board
+censuses. Exact original runner bytes for both are retained. Later guard and
+reporting changes have focused tests; each real launch qualifies actual RSS
+sampling before any scientific identity is claimed.
+
+The separate, prospectively fixed anonymous engineering exercise used three
+seeds101/102/103 and1024 actions each, with private signal-coordinate permutations,
+two nuisance bits and selected-action-only XOR feedback. They admitted28/26/24
+conditions and received911/923/838 nonzero scoring-credit receipts. Final strict
+greedy choices were16/16,16/16,8/16 across four contexts and four nuisance values.
+No seed or parameter was changed in response. This establishes a working
+discovery/credit path and preserves incomplete learning in one case; it does not
+establish that this selector outperforms random admission or will solve chess.
+
+## Fixed scientific work
+
+- One fresh seed:202610210901. It has not been used by engineering. The exclusive
+  persistent identity claim precedes actor creation and is never cleared after
+  a failed attempt.
+- Exactly3072 real one-White-move training actions:2048 acquisition plus1024
+  continuation. No performance-dependent extension, retry, replacement seed,
+  changed constants or installed fitted weights.
+- The known1512-position M1 population is exported as FEN strings only from the
+  two pinned existing regression files. Correct moves/rewards in those files
+  are not passed to the organism. This is known-population development evidence,
+  not unseen-position generalization.
+- An independent seeded coach RNG draws a population index uniformly per action;
+  learner topology, residuals, trials and outcomes never alter this schedule.
+- The existing chess feature port supplies only declared current-board/candidate
+  measurements. The native graph selects and actually executes one legal move.
+  Feedback is+1 for its observed checkmate,-1 otherwise. No alternative outcome,
+  mate-in-0 lesson, teacher recognizer, after-state evaluator or strategic label
+  enters discovery.
+- Nonlearning full1512-position greedy censuses at0/1536/2048/3072, each through a
+  disposable copy. Training state and RNG must remain unchanged by evaluations.
+- Checkpoints at0/512/1024/1536/2048/2560/3072. Save the complete opaque object,
+  its transport hash, the declared behavioral/development snapshot and schedule.
+
+## Measurements and verdict
+
+Primary descriptive output is census coverage out of1512 and its solved-row
+transitions. Report acquisition at sampled1536/2048 and continuation retention
+at3072, including losses as well as gains. Matching the full M1 benchmark means
+1512/1512 at all three noninitial censuses; a lesser score remains a valid
+exploratory result, not something to rerun or tune away.
+
+Report physical nodes, binding slots, distinct live/trial reader definitions,
+scoring conditions, parameter count and development history separately. Separate
+prospectively scored admissions from exploratory admissions, including those with
+no completed later review. Count actual post-birth active updates and retirements.
+Predictive relevance is not automatically policy value or causal usefulness.
+The first study has no matched random arm and cannot identify selector advantage.
+
+Independent native generative reconstruction must reproduce every training
+action/outcome, learning receipt, lifecycle event, checkpoint snapshot and census.
+Independent scalar arithmetic checks bias and active fast increments, unchanged
+inactive/slow coefficients at credit stage and the saved native prediction sum.
+Restore all own checkpoints after checking their transport hashes; verify the
+next saved transition from the six nonterminal cold checkpoints. This checks the
+declared state and continuation, not a claim to compare every transient physical
+node field in an independently implemented verifier.
+
+An actual source, semantic, integrity or resource failure stops the attempt and
+retains a partial result. Technical censoring is distinct from learning failure.
+No practical learning verdict is accepted before full declared reconstruction.
+
+## Resources and execution
+
+Use the explicit project Python3.12 environment, isolated worktree src and
+libs/recon-lite/src, one numerical thread and at most one native worker. Pin
+actual runtime dependencies and the runner after the prospective source commit.
+Do not hash or copy all historical studies.
+
+The launcher has a four-hour ceiling from its own invocation, including production,
+replay and checksum readback. It reserves the second real replay pass and five
+minutes for completion reporting. Each worker is sampled against2GiB RSS, with
+actual sampling permission qualified before scientific initialization. A live
+worker with unavailable RSS sampling aborts. These are sampled limits and
+empirical engineering checks, not a theorem about peak memory or every reachable
+future graph. The learner separately enforces8192 physical nodes.
+
+The32-action engineering path does not measure the largest future grown graph.
+It establishes execution and reconstruction mechanics; a genuine later growth
+cost failure will be reported as such rather than used to waive checks. Preserve
+all records and source hashes on interruption. A task-owned idle-sleep assertion
+may run and is cleaned at exit. No global power settings or external storage
+reorganization is needed.
+
+The exact output is
+/Users/banquo/Documents/ChatGPT/Hector-Recon/sparse-terminal-discovery-20261021-evidence/m1-pilot-901.
+The launcher refuses an existing output or previously consumed scientific seed.
+At completion retain compact full records, seven checkpoints, censuses, source
+pins, actual resource receipts, reconstruction and checksum readback. Do not
+introduce another archive/qualification framework.
+
+Stop after this attempt and its report. No further cohort, new credit law,
+mate-in-0 classifier, M2 integration, merge, push or default adoption follows
+automatically, regardless of score.
